    <!-- ==========================================
         INTRODUCTION
    =========================================== -->

    <p>

        Data Interpretation (DI) is an important section in
        placement exams. It tests your ability to understand,
        analyze, and solve problems based on data presented in
        tables, bar graphs, pie charts, line graphs, and charts.

        Companies use DI questions to evaluate your analytical
        and decision-making skills.

    </p>


